## Part 2: Privacy Policy

### 1. Summary
Cyber Save has no user accounts and no servers of its own. Downloaded media stays on your device. To work, the app does share some data with the services described below.

### 2. Data the App Handles

**Links you paste or share into the app**
To find the media behind a link, the app sends that link to the platform it belongs to (for example Instagram, TikTok, X/Twitter, Facebook, Reddit, Pinterest, Vimeo, Dailymotion, Twitch, Bilibili, VK, Bluesky, Threads, Snapchat, Streamable). For some platforms the link is also sent to third-party download or proxy services, including: tikwm.com, snapsave.app, fdownloader.net, getfvid.com, fdown.net, api.fxtwitter.com, api.vxtwitter.com, api.allorigins.win and r.jina.ai. Those services receive the link and your IP address and are governed by their own privacy policies.

**Instagram sign-in (optional)**
If you choose to sign in to Instagram, you do so on Instagram's own login page inside the app. The app never sees your password. It keeps Instagram's session cookies, encrypted in your device's secure storage (Android Keystore / iOS Keychain), and sends them **only to Instagram** to fetch media you request. You can sign out at any time in Settings, which deletes the stored session. Automated access may be restricted by Instagram; use this feature at your own risk.

**Torrents (BitTorrent)**
When you add a magnet link or .torrent file, the app joins the public BitTorrent network. As with any BitTorrent client, **your IP address is visible to other peers and to trackers** in that torrent's swarm, and pieces you have downloaded may be uploaded to other peers. Torrent metadata may be fetched from public torrent-cache services (e.g. itorrents.org). The torrent engine runs locally on your device and is not reachable from other devices.

**Data stored on your device**
Download history, link history, settings and downloaded files are stored locally. They are excluded from cloud backup and device transfer, and are deleted when you uninstall the app (downloaded files saved to your gallery remain there).

